%%report admission-offer-by-status title: Admission Offers by status entity: AdmissionOffer chart: pie x: status y: records help: Authorized offer of a seat to an applicant with an expiration date. How admission offers divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_admission_offer WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report admission-offer-lifecycle title: Admission Offer lifecycle entity: AdmissionOffer chart: bar x: state y: records help: Authorized offer of a seat to an applicant with an expiration date. Where admission offers sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'issued', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'accepted', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'declined', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'expired', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'withdrawn', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_admission_offer WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
