%%report entrance-exam-result-per-entrance-exam title: Entrance Exam Results per entrance exam entity: EntranceExamResult chart: bar x: entrance_exam y: records help: Candidate-specific examination outcome. Which entrance exam the most entrance exam results belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS entrance_exam, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_entrance_exam_result x LEFT JOIN bus_entrance_exam p ON p.id = x.entrance_exam_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report entrance-exam-result-marks-per-entrance-exam title: Total marks per entrance exam entity: EntranceExamResult chart: bar x: entrance_exam y: total_marks help: Candidate-specific examination outcome. Entrance Exam Results added up on marks for each entrance exam, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS entrance_exam, ROUND(SUM(x.marks)::numeric, 2) AS total_marks FROM bus_entrance_exam_result x LEFT JOIN bus_entrance_exam p ON p.id = x.entrance_exam_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report scholarship-application-by-status title: Scholarship Applications by status entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: pie x: status y: records help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. How scholarship applications divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_scholarship_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report scholarship-application-lifecycle title: Scholarship Application lifecycle entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: bar x: state y: records help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. Where scholarship applications sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'aid_requested' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_under_review', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_awarded', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_declined', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_withdrawn', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_scholarship_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report scholarship-application-requested-amount-by-status title: Total requested amount by status entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: bar x: status y: total_requested_amount help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. Scholarship Applications added up on requested amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(requested_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_requested_amount FROM bus_scholarship_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report scholarship-application-requested-amount-per-month title: Average requested amount per month entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: line x: month y: average_requested_amount help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. The average requested amount of scholarship applications created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(requested_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_requested_amount FROM bus_scholarship_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report scholarship-application-largest-by-requested-amount title: The ten largest scholarship applications by requested amount entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: bar x: record y: requested_amount help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. The records with the highest requested amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT status::text AS record, requested_amount FROM bus_scholarship_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND requested_amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY requested_amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report scholarship-application-per-admission-application title: Scholarship Applications per admission application entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: bar x: admission_application y: records help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. Which admission application the most scholarship applications belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.application_number::text, '(none)') AS admission_application, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_scholarship_application x LEFT JOIN bus_admission_application p ON p.id = x.admission_application_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report scholarship-application-requested-amount-per-admission-application title: Total requested amount per admission application entity: ScholarshipApplication chart: bar x: admission_application y: total_requested_amount help: Learner request for institution-sponsored financial assistance. Scholarship Applications added up on requested amount for each admission application, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.application_number::text, '(none)') AS admission_application, ROUND(SUM(x.requested_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_requested_amount FROM bus_scholarship_application x LEFT JOIN bus_admission_application p ON p.id = x.admission_application_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report learning-catalog-created-per-month title: Learning Catalogs created per month entity: LearningCatalog chart: line x: month y: records help: Published set of current educational offerings; publication does not imply a student is registered or meets entry requirements. New learning catalogs per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_learning_catalog WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report learning-catalog-age-bands title: How recently learning catalogs were changed entity: LearningCatalog chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Published set of current educational offerings; publication does not imply a student is registered or meets entry requirements. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_learning_catalog WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report learning-catalog-per-institution title: Learning Catalogs per institution entity: LearningCatalog chart: bar x: institution y: records help: Published set of current educational offerings; publication does not imply a student is registered or meets entry requirements. Which institution the most learning catalogs belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS institution, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_learning_catalog x LEFT JOIN bus_institution p ON p.id = x.institution_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
