%%report academic-term-enrollment-by-status title: Academic Term Enrollments by status entity: AcademicTermEnrollment chart: pie x: status y: records help: Formal registration of a student for an academic term. How academic term enrollments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_academic_term_enrollment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report academic-term-enrollment-lifecycle title: Academic Term Enrollment lifecycle entity: AcademicTermEnrollment chart: bar x: state y: records help: Formal registration of a student for an academic term. Where academic term enrollments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'term_requested' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'term_registered', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'term_active', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'term_completed', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'term_cancelled', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_academic_term_enrollment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report academic-term-enrollment-per-learner-profile title: Academic Term Enrollments per learner profile entity: AcademicTermEnrollment chart: bar x: learner_profile y: records help: Formal registration of a student for an academic term. Which learner profile the most academic term enrollments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.learner_number::text, '(none)') AS learner_profile, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_academic_term_enrollment x LEFT JOIN bus_learner_profile p ON p.id = x.learner_profile_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report course-enrollment-by-status title: Course Enrollments by status entity: CourseEnrollment chart: pie x: status y: records help: Learner registration in a scheduled offering. How course enrollments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_course_enrollment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report course-enrollment-lifecycle title: Course Enrollment lifecycle entity: CourseEnrollment chart: bar x: state y: records help: Learner registration in a scheduled offering. Where course enrollments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'registered', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'completed', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'failed', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'withdrawn', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_course_enrollment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report course-enrollment-per-learner-profile title: Course Enrollments per learner profile entity: CourseEnrollment chart: bar x: learner_profile y: records help: Learner registration in a scheduled offering. Which learner profile the most course enrollments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.learner_number::text, '(none)') AS learner_profile, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_course_enrollment x LEFT JOIN bus_learner_profile p ON p.id = x.learner_profile_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report waitlist-entry-by-priority title: Waitlist Entries by priority entity: WaitlistEntry chart: pie x: priority y: records help: Ordered request for a full course offering. How waitlist entries divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_waitlist_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report waitlist-entry-priority-by-priority title: Total priority by priority entity: WaitlistEntry chart: bar x: priority y: total_priority help: Ordered request for a full course offering. Waitlist Entries added up on priority, split by priority, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, ROUND(SUM(priority)::numeric, 2) AS total_priority FROM bus_waitlist_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report waitlist-entry-priority-per-month title: Average priority per month entity: WaitlistEntry chart: line x: month y: average_priority help: Ordered request for a full course offering. The average priority of waitlist entries created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(priority)::numeric, 2) AS average_priority FROM bus_waitlist_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
