%%report success-goal-largest-by-progress-pct title: The ten largest success goals by progress pct entity: SuccessGoal chart: bar x: record y: progress_pct help: Measurable objective inside a student success plan. The records with the highest progress pct; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, progress_pct FROM bus_success_goal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND progress_pct IS NOT NULL ORDER BY progress_pct DESC LIMIT 10
%%report success-goal-per-student-success-plan title: Success Goals per student success plan entity: SuccessGoal chart: bar x: student_success_plan y: records help: Measurable objective inside a student success plan. Which student success plan the most success goals belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS student_success_plan, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_success_goal x LEFT JOIN bus_student_success_plan p ON p.id = x.student_success_plan_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report success-goal-progress-pct-per-student-success-plan title: Total progress pct per student success plan entity: SuccessGoal chart: bar x: student_success_plan y: total_progress_pct help: Measurable objective inside a student success plan. Success Goals added up on progress pct for each student success plan, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS student_success_plan, ROUND(SUM(x.progress_pct)::numeric, 2) AS total_progress_pct FROM bus_success_goal x LEFT JOIN bus_student_success_plan p ON p.id = x.student_success_plan_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report student-alert-by-status title: Student Alerts by status entity: StudentAlert chart: pie x: status y: records help: Risk signal identified from attendance, academic or welfare evidence; triage is required before taking adverse action. How student alerts divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_alert WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report student-alert-by-alert-type title: Student Alerts by alert type entity: StudentAlert chart: pie x: alert_type y: records help: Risk signal identified from attendance, academic or welfare evidence; triage is required before taking adverse action. How student alerts divide across alert type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(alert_type::text, '(unset)') AS alert_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_alert WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report student-alert-lifecycle title: Student Alert lifecycle entity: StudentAlert chart: bar x: state y: records help: Risk signal identified from attendance, academic or welfare evidence; triage is required before taking adverse action. Where student alerts sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'alert_new' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'alert_triaged', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'alert_actioned', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'alert_dismissed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_alert WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report student-case-by-status title: Student Cases by status entity: StudentCase chart: pie x: status y: records help: Confidential request for student support with ownership, triage, intervention and resolution. How student cases divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report student-case-by-priority title: Student Cases by priority entity: StudentCase chart: pie x: priority y: records help: Confidential request for student support with ownership, triage, intervention and resolution. How student cases divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report student-case-by-case-type title: Student Cases by case type entity: StudentCase chart: pie x: case_type y: records help: Confidential request for student support with ownership, triage, intervention and resolution. How student cases divide across case type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(case_type::text, '(unset)') AS case_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report student-case-lifecycle title: Student Case lifecycle entity: StudentCase chart: bar x: state y: records help: Confidential request for student support with ownership, triage, intervention and resolution. Where student cases sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'open', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'triaged', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'in_progress', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'resolved', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_student_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
