%%report service-appointment-per-appointment-type title: Service Appointments per appointment type entity: ServiceAppointment chart: bar x: appointment_type y: records help: Reserved meeting between students and institutional resources. Which appointment type the most service appointments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS appointment_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_appointment x LEFT JOIN bus_appointment_type p ON p.id = x.appointment_type_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report appointment-attendee-by-attendance-status title: Appointment Attendees by attendance status entity: AppointmentAttendee chart: pie x: attendance_status y: records help: Participant invited or expected at a scheduled meeting; replies and no-shows are reported without rewriting the appointment. How appointment attendees divide across attendance status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(attendance_status::text, '(unset)') AS attendance_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment_attendee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-attendee-per-service-appointment title: Appointment Attendees per service appointment entity: AppointmentAttendee chart: bar x: service_appointment y: records help: Participant invited or expected at a scheduled meeting; replies and no-shows are reported without rewriting the appointment. Which service appointment the most appointment attendees belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.status::text, '(none)') AS service_appointment, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment_attendee x LEFT JOIN bus_service_appointment p ON p.id = x.service_appointment_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report appointment-attendee-per-person title: Appointment Attendees per person entity: AppointmentAttendee chart: bar x: person y: records help: Participant invited or expected at a scheduled meeting; replies and no-shows are reported without rewriting the appointment. Which person the most appointment attendees belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.email::text, '(none)') AS person, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment_attendee x LEFT JOIN bus_person p ON p.id = x.person_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report appointment-waitlist-by-priority title: Appointment Waitlists by priority entity: AppointmentWaitlist chart: pie x: priority y: records help: Ordered request for an unavailable student service appointment. How appointment waitlists divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment_waitlist WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-waitlist-priority-by-priority title: Total priority by priority (Appointment Waitlist) entity: AppointmentWaitlist chart: bar x: priority y: total_priority help: Ordered request for an unavailable student service appointment. Appointment Waitlists added up on priority, split by priority, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, ROUND(SUM(priority)::numeric, 2) AS total_priority FROM bus_appointment_waitlist WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report appointment-waitlist-priority-per-month title: Average priority per month (Appointment Waitlist) entity: AppointmentWaitlist chart: line x: month y: average_priority help: Ordered request for an unavailable student service appointment. The average priority of appointment waitlists created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(priority)::numeric, 2) AS average_priority FROM bus_appointment_waitlist WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report access-role-by-scope-type title: Access Roles by scope type entity: AccessRole chart: pie x: scope_type y: records help: Institution-approved access profile that describes staff responsibilities; application rights require scoped assignments. How access roles divide across scope type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(scope_type::text, '(unset)') AS scope_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_access_role WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report access-role-created-per-month title: Access Roles created per month entity: AccessRole chart: line x: month y: records help: Institution-approved access profile that describes staff responsibilities; application rights require scoped assignments. New access roles per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_access_role WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report access-role-per-institution title: Access Roles per institution entity: AccessRole chart: bar x: institution y: records help: Institution-approved access profile that describes staff responsibilities; application rights require scoped assignments. Which institution the most access roles belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS institution, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_access_role x LEFT JOIN bus_institution p ON p.id = x.institution_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report role-assignment-per-access-role title: Role Assignments per access role entity: RoleAssignment chart: bar x: access_role y: records help: Time-bounded assignment of an institutional access role to a user at a particular campus, department or course scope. Which access role the most role assignments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS access_role, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_role_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_access_role p ON p.id = x.access_role_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report role-assignment-per-user title: Role Assignments per user entity: RoleAssignment chart: bar x: user y: records help: Time-bounded assignment of an institutional access role to a user at a particular campus, department or course scope. Which user the most role assignments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.email::text, '(none)') AS user, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_role_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_user p ON p.id = x.user_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report role-assignment-per-campus title: Role Assignments per campus entity: RoleAssignment chart: bar x: campus y: records help: Time-bounded assignment of an institutional access role to a user at a particular campus, department or course scope. Which campus the most role assignments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS campus, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_role_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_campus p ON p.id = x.campus_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report academic-access-grant-by-access-level title: Academic Access Grants by access level entity: AcademicAccessGrant chart: pie x: access_level y: records help: Scoped permission to see or change academic records for an assigned faculty or support role. How academic access grants divide across access level, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(access_level::text, '(unset)') AS access_level, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_academic_access_grant WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report academic-access-grant-per-course-offering title: Academic Access Grants per course offering entity: AcademicAccessGrant chart: bar x: course_offering y: records help: Scoped permission to see or change academic records for an assigned faculty or support role. Which course offering the most academic access grants belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.section_code::text, '(none)') AS course_offering, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_academic_access_grant x LEFT JOIN bus_course_offering p ON p.id = x.course_offering_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report academic-access-grant-per-learner-profile title: Academic Access Grants per learner profile entity: AcademicAccessGrant chart: bar x: learner_profile y: records help: Scoped permission to see or change academic records for an assigned faculty or support role. Which learner profile the most academic access grants belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.learner_number::text, '(none)') AS learner_profile, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_academic_access_grant x LEFT JOIN bus_learner_profile p ON p.id = x.learner_profile_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report tuition-plan-standard-amount-per-month title: Average standard amount per month entity: TuitionPlan chart: line x: month y: average_standard_amount help: Published pricing policy for a program and intake; effective terms must be protected from retrospective edits. The average standard amount of tuition plans created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(standard_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_standard_amount FROM bus_tuition_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report tuition-plan-largest-by-standard-amount title: The ten largest tuition plans by standard amount entity: TuitionPlan chart: bar x: record y: standard_amount help: Published pricing policy for a program and intake; effective terms must be protected from retrospective edits. The records with the highest standard amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, standard_amount FROM bus_tuition_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND standard_amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY standard_amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report tuition-plan-top-currency-code title: Tuition Plans: the most common currency code entity: TuitionPlan chart: bar x: currency_code y: records help: Published pricing policy for a program and intake; effective terms must be protected from retrospective edits. The ten most frequent values of currency code among tuition plans; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency_code, '(blank)') AS currency_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_tuition_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
