%%report student-payment-largest-by-amount title: The ten largest student payments by amount entity: StudentPayment chart: bar x: record y: amount help: Receipt of learner funds with settlement evidence. The records with the highest amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT payment_reference::text AS record, amount FROM bus_student_payment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report payment-allocation-allocated-amount-per-month title: Average allocated amount per month entity: PaymentAllocation chart: line x: month y: average_allocated_amount help: Portion of a receipt applied to a specific invoice; allocations cannot exceed either settled funds or outstanding balance. The average allocated amount of payment allocations created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(allocated_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_allocated_amount FROM bus_payment_allocation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report payment-allocation-per-student-payment title: Payment Allocations per student payment entity: PaymentAllocation chart: bar x: student_payment y: records help: Portion of a receipt applied to a specific invoice; allocations cannot exceed either settled funds or outstanding balance. Which student payment the most payment allocations belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.payment_reference::text, '(none)') AS student_payment, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_payment_allocation x LEFT JOIN bus_student_payment p ON p.id = x.student_payment_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report payment-allocation-allocated-amount-per-student-payment title: Total allocated amount per student payment entity: PaymentAllocation chart: bar x: student_payment y: total_allocated_amount help: Portion of a receipt applied to a specific invoice; allocations cannot exceed either settled funds or outstanding balance. Payment Allocations added up on allocated amount for each student payment, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.payment_reference::text, '(none)') AS student_payment, ROUND(SUM(x.allocated_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_allocated_amount FROM bus_payment_allocation x LEFT JOIN bus_student_payment p ON p.id = x.student_payment_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report refund-request-by-status title: Refund Requests by status entity: RefundRequest chart: pie x: status y: records help: Formal request to return student money after validating original settlement, eligibility and approval. How refund requests divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_refund_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report refund-request-lifecycle title: Refund Request lifecycle entity: RefundRequest chart: bar x: state y: records help: Formal request to return student money after validating original settlement, eligibility and approval. Where refund requests sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'refund_requested' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'refund_reviewed', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'refund_approved', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'refund_rejected', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'refund_processed', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_refund_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report refund-request-amount-by-status title: Total amount by status (Refund Request) entity: RefundRequest chart: bar x: status y: total_amount help: Formal request to return student money after validating original settlement, eligibility and approval. Refund Requests added up on amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_refund_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report refund-request-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (Refund Request) entity: RefundRequest chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: Formal request to return student money after validating original settlement, eligibility and approval. The average amount of refund requests created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_refund_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report scholarship-by-scholarship-type title: Scholarships by scholarship type entity: Scholarship chart: pie x: scholarship_type y: records help: Published institutional funding award with eligibility criteria and a controlled financial budget. How scholarships divide across scholarship type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(scholarship_type::text, '(unset)') AS scholarship_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_scholarship WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report scholarship-budget-amount-by-scholarship-type title: Total budget amount by scholarship type entity: Scholarship chart: bar x: scholarship_type y: total_budget_amount help: Published institutional funding award with eligibility criteria and a controlled financial budget. Scholarships added up on budget amount, split by scholarship type, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(scholarship_type::text, '(unset)') AS scholarship_type, ROUND(SUM(budget_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_budget_amount FROM bus_scholarship WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report scholarship-budget-amount-per-month title: Average budget amount per month entity: Scholarship chart: line x: month y: average_budget_amount help: Published institutional funding award with eligibility criteria and a controlled financial budget. The average budget amount of scholarships created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(budget_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_budget_amount FROM bus_scholarship WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report scholarship-award-by-approval-status title: Scholarship Awards by approval status entity: ScholarshipAward chart: pie x: approval_status y: records help: Award to a student from an approved scholarship pool. How scholarship awards divide across approval status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(approval_status::text, '(unset)') AS approval_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_scholarship_award WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report scholarship-award-awarded-amount-by-approval-status title: Total awarded amount by approval status entity: ScholarshipAward chart: bar x: approval_status y: total_awarded_amount help: Award to a student from an approved scholarship pool. Scholarship Awards added up on awarded amount, split by approval status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(approval_status::text, '(unset)') AS approval_status, ROUND(SUM(awarded_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_awarded_amount FROM bus_scholarship_award WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report scholarship-award-awarded-amount-per-month title: Average awarded amount per month entity: ScholarshipAward chart: line x: month y: average_awarded_amount help: Award to a student from an approved scholarship pool. The average awarded amount of scholarship awards created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(awarded_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_awarded_amount FROM bus_scholarship_award WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report financial-aid-disbursement-by-status title: Financial Aid Disbursements by status entity: FinancialAidDisbursement chart: pie x: status y: records help: Scheduled transfer of approved student aid, subject to payment confirmation and institutional funding controls. How financial aid disbursements divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_aid_disbursement WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report financial-aid-disbursement-lifecycle title: Financial Aid Disbursement lifecycle entity: FinancialAidDisbursement chart: bar x: state y: records help: Scheduled transfer of approved student aid, subject to payment confirmation and institutional funding controls. Where financial aid disbursements sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'aid_planned' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_authorized', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_sent', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_confirmed', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'aid_failed', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_aid_disbursement WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report financial-aid-disbursement-amount-by-status title: Total amount by status (Financial Aid Disbursement) entity: FinancialAidDisbursement chart: bar x: status y: total_amount help: Scheduled transfer of approved student aid, subject to payment confirmation and institutional funding controls. Financial Aid Disbursements added up on amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_financial_aid_disbursement WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report payment-plan-by-status title: Payment Plans by status entity: PaymentPlan chart: pie x: status y: records help: Agreed installment arrangement for student charges. How payment plans divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_payment_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report payment-plan-installments-by-status title: Total installments by status entity: PaymentPlan chart: bar x: status y: total_installments help: Agreed installment arrangement for student charges. Payment Plans added up on installments, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(installments)::numeric, 2) AS total_installments FROM bus_payment_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report payment-plan-installments-per-month title: Average installments per month entity: PaymentPlan chart: line x: month y: average_installments help: Agreed installment arrangement for student charges. The average installments of payment plans created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(installments)::numeric, 2) AS average_installments FROM bus_payment_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report payment-installment-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (Payment Installment) entity: PaymentInstallment chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: Due amount on a student payment plan, used to identify scheduled obligations and missed installments. The average amount of payment installments created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_payment_installment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report payment-installment-settled-amount-per-month title: Average settled amount per month entity: PaymentInstallment chart: line x: month y: average_settled_amount help: Due amount on a student payment plan, used to identify scheduled obligations and missed installments. The average settled amount of payment installments created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(settled_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_settled_amount FROM bus_payment_installment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report payment-installment-per-payment-plan title: Payment Installments per payment plan entity: PaymentInstallment chart: bar x: payment_plan y: records help: Due amount on a student payment plan, used to identify scheduled obligations and missed installments. Which payment plan the most payment installments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS payment_plan, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_payment_installment x LEFT JOIN bus_payment_plan p ON p.id = x.payment_plan_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report corporate-partner-by-partner-status title: Corporate Partners by partner status entity: CorporatePartner chart: pie x: partner_status y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. How corporate partners divide across partner status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(partner_status::text, '(unset)') AS partner_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report corporate-partner-created-per-month title: Corporate Partners created per month entity: CorporatePartner chart: line x: month y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. New corporate partners per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report corporate-partner-created-by-weekday title: Corporate Partners created by day of the week entity: CorporatePartner chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. Which days corporate partners are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report corporate-partner-changed-per-month title: Corporate Partners last changed per month entity: CorporatePartner chart: line x: month y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. How recently corporate partners were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report corporate-partner-age-bands title: How recently corporate partners were changed entity: CorporatePartner chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report corporate-partner-per-institution title: Corporate Partners per institution entity: CorporatePartner chart: bar x: institution y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. Which institution the most corporate partners belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS institution, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner x LEFT JOIN bus_institution p ON p.id = x.institution_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report corporate-partner-top-industry title: Corporate Partners: the most common industry entity: CorporatePartner chart: bar x: industry y: records help: Employer or industry organization collaborating on internships, placements, research or educational services. The ten most frequent values of industry among corporate partners; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(industry, '(blank)') AS industry, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corporate_partner WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
