%%report placement-opportunity-closes-on-per-month title: Placement Opportunities by closes on entity: PlacementOpportunity chart: line x: month y: records help: Employer opening offered to eligible learners with capacity and recruitment deadline. Placement Opportunities grouped by the month of closes on, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', closes_on), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_placement_opportunity WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND closes_on IS NOT NULL AND closes_on >= now() - interval '24 months' AND closes_on < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report placement-opportunity-vacancies-by-status title: Total vacancies by status entity: PlacementOpportunity chart: bar x: status y: total_vacancies help: Employer opening offered to eligible learners with capacity and recruitment deadline. Placement Opportunities added up on vacancies, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(vacancies)::numeric, 2) AS total_vacancies FROM bus_placement_opportunity WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report placement-opportunity-vacancies-per-month title: Average vacancies per month entity: PlacementOpportunity chart: line x: month y: average_vacancies help: Employer opening offered to eligible learners with capacity and recruitment deadline. The average vacancies of placement opportunities created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(vacancies)::numeric, 2) AS average_vacancies FROM bus_placement_opportunity WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report placement-opportunity-largest-by-vacancies title: The ten largest placement opportunities by vacancies entity: PlacementOpportunity chart: bar x: record y: vacancies help: Employer opening offered to eligible learners with capacity and recruitment deadline. The records with the highest vacancies; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT title::text AS record, vacancies FROM bus_placement_opportunity WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND vacancies IS NOT NULL ORDER BY vacancies DESC LIMIT 10
%%report placement-opportunity-per-corporate-partner title: Placement Opportunities per corporate partner entity: PlacementOpportunity chart: bar x: corporate_partner y: records help: Employer opening offered to eligible learners with capacity and recruitment deadline. Which corporate partner the most placement opportunities belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS corporate_partner, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_placement_opportunity x LEFT JOIN bus_corporate_partner p ON p.id = x.corporate_partner_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report placement-opportunity-vacancies-per-corporate-partner title: Total vacancies per corporate partner entity: PlacementOpportunity chart: bar x: corporate_partner y: total_vacancies help: Employer opening offered to eligible learners with capacity and recruitment deadline. Placement Opportunities added up on vacancies for each corporate partner, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS corporate_partner, ROUND(SUM(x.vacancies)::numeric, 2) AS total_vacancies FROM bus_placement_opportunity x LEFT JOIN bus_corporate_partner p ON p.id = x.corporate_partner_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report placement-application-by-application-status title: Placement Applications by application status entity: PlacementApplication chart: pie x: application_status y: records help: Student candidacy for a placement, tracked separately from the employer opportunity. How placement applications divide across application status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(application_status::text, '(unset)') AS application_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_placement_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report placement-application-created-per-month title: Placement Applications created per month entity: PlacementApplication chart: line x: month y: records help: Student candidacy for a placement, tracked separately from the employer opportunity. New placement applications per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_placement_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report placement-application-age-bands title: How recently placement applications were changed entity: PlacementApplication chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Student candidacy for a placement, tracked separately from the employer opportunity. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_placement_application WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
