%%report residence-per-campus title: Residences per campus entity: Residence chart: bar x: campus y: records help: Student accommodation building managed by the institution, with occupancy and safety controls. Which campus the most residences belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS campus, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_residence x LEFT JOIN bus_campus p ON p.id = x.campus_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report residence-room-by-occupancy-status title: Residence Rooms by occupancy status entity: ResidenceRoom chart: pie x: occupancy_status y: records help: Allocatable residence room whose capacity and accessibility features constrain assignments. How residence rooms divide across occupancy status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(occupancy_status::text, '(unset)') AS occupancy_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_residence_room WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report residence-room-beds-by-occupancy-status title: Total beds by occupancy status entity: ResidenceRoom chart: bar x: occupancy_status y: total_beds help: Allocatable residence room whose capacity and accessibility features constrain assignments. Residence Rooms added up on beds, split by occupancy status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(occupancy_status::text, '(unset)') AS occupancy_status, ROUND(SUM(beds)::numeric, 2) AS total_beds FROM bus_residence_room WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report residence-room-beds-per-month title: Average beds per month entity: ResidenceRoom chart: line x: month y: average_beds help: Allocatable residence room whose capacity and accessibility features constrain assignments. The average beds of residence rooms created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(beds)::numeric, 2) AS average_beds FROM bus_residence_room WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report residence-room-largest-by-beds title: The ten largest residence rooms by beds entity: ResidenceRoom chart: bar x: record y: beds help: Allocatable residence room whose capacity and accessibility features constrain assignments. The records with the highest beds; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, beds FROM bus_residence_room WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND beds IS NOT NULL ORDER BY beds DESC LIMIT 10
%%report residence-room-per-residence title: Residence Rooms per residence entity: ResidenceRoom chart: bar x: residence y: records help: Allocatable residence room whose capacity and accessibility features constrain assignments. Which residence the most residence rooms belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS residence, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_residence_room x LEFT JOIN bus_residence p ON p.id = x.residence_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report residence-room-beds-per-residence title: Total beds per residence entity: ResidenceRoom chart: bar x: residence y: total_beds help: Allocatable residence room whose capacity and accessibility features constrain assignments. Residence Rooms added up on beds for each residence, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS residence, ROUND(SUM(x.beds)::numeric, 2) AS total_beds FROM bus_residence_room x LEFT JOIN bus_residence p ON p.id = x.residence_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report residence-assignment-by-status title: Residence Assignments by status entity: ResidenceAssignment chart: pie x: status y: records help: Specific student occupancy of a residence room, with check-in, check-out and billing implications. How residence assignments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_residence_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report residence-assignment-lifecycle title: Residence Assignment lifecycle entity: ResidenceAssignment chart: bar x: state y: records help: Specific student occupancy of a residence room, with check-in, check-out and billing implications. Where residence assignments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'housing_requested' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'housing_assigned', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'housing_checked_in', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'housing_checked_out', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'housing_cancelled', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_residence_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report residence-assignment-per-residence-room title: Residence Assignments per residence room entity: ResidenceAssignment chart: bar x: residence_room y: records help: Specific student occupancy of a residence room, with check-in, check-out and billing implications. Which residence room the most residence assignments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS residence_room, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_residence_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_residence_room p ON p.id = x.residence_room_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report transport-route-by-service-type title: Transport Routes by service type entity: TransportRoute chart: pie x: service_type y: records help: Campus transport service definition with scheduled stops and accessibility category. How transport routes divide across service type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(service_type::text, '(unset)') AS service_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_route WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report transport-route-created-per-month title: Transport Routes created per month entity: TransportRoute chart: line x: month y: records help: Campus transport service definition with scheduled stops and accessibility category. New transport routes per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_route WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transport-route-per-campus title: Transport Routes per campus entity: TransportRoute chart: bar x: campus y: records help: Campus transport service definition with scheduled stops and accessibility category. Which campus the most transport routes belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS campus, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_route x LEFT JOIN bus_campus p ON p.id = x.campus_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report transport-stop-created-per-month title: Transport Stops created per month entity: TransportStop chart: line x: month y: records help: Boarding location and order on a transport route. New transport stops per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_stop WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transport-stop-arrival-time-per-month title: Transport Stops by arrival time entity: TransportStop chart: line x: month y: records help: Boarding location and order on a transport route. Transport Stops grouped by the month of arrival time, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', arrival_time), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_stop WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND arrival_time IS NOT NULL AND arrival_time >= now() - interval '24 months' AND arrival_time < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transport-stop-per-transport-route title: Transport Stops per transport route entity: TransportStop chart: bar x: transport_route y: records help: Boarding location and order on a transport route. Which transport route the most transport stops belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS transport_route, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_stop x LEFT JOIN bus_transport_route p ON p.id = x.transport_route_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report transport-assignment-by-status title: Transport Assignments by status entity: TransportAssignment chart: pie x: status y: records help: Student entitlement to use a transport route during effective dates, not a GPS tracking record. How transport assignments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report transport-assignment-lifecycle title: Transport Assignment lifecycle entity: TransportAssignment chart: bar x: state y: records help: Student entitlement to use a transport route during effective dates, not a GPS tracking record. Where transport assignments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'transport_requested' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'transport_approved', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'transport_active', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'transport_expired', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'transport_cancelled', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report transport-assignment-per-transport-route title: Transport Assignments per transport route entity: TransportAssignment chart: bar x: transport_route y: records help: Student entitlement to use a transport route during effective dates, not a GPS tracking record. Which transport route the most transport assignments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS transport_route, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transport_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_transport_route p ON p.id = x.transport_route_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report supplier-created-per-month title: Suppliers created per month entity: Supplier chart: line x: month y: records help: Approved supplier for campus purchases, with commercial terms and procurement responsibility. New suppliers per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report supplier-age-bands title: How recently suppliers were changed entity: Supplier chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Approved supplier for campus purchases, with commercial terms and procurement responsibility. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report supplier-per-institution title: Suppliers per institution entity: Supplier chart: bar x: institution y: records help: Approved supplier for campus purchases, with commercial terms and procurement responsibility. Which institution the most suppliers belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS institution, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier x LEFT JOIN bus_institution p ON p.id = x.institution_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report purchase-order-by-status title: Purchase Orders by status entity: PurchaseOrder chart: pie x: status y: records help: Authorized commitment to buy goods or services. How purchase orders divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_purchase_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report purchase-order-lifecycle title: Purchase Order lifecycle entity: PurchaseOrder chart: bar x: state y: records help: Authorized commitment to buy goods or services. Where purchase orders sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'po_draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'po_submitted', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'po_approved', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'po_received', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'po_cancelled', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_purchase_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report purchase-order-total-by-status title: Total total by status (Purchase Order) entity: PurchaseOrder chart: bar x: status y: total_total help: Authorized commitment to buy goods or services. Purchase Orders added up on total, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(total)::numeric, 2) AS total_total FROM bus_purchase_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report purchase-order-total-per-month title: Average total per month (Purchase Order) entity: PurchaseOrder chart: line x: month y: average_total help: Authorized commitment to buy goods or services. The average total of purchase orders created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(total)::numeric, 2) AS average_total FROM bus_purchase_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report purchase-order-largest-by-total title: The ten largest purchase orders by total entity: PurchaseOrder chart: bar x: record y: total help: Authorized commitment to buy goods or services. The records with the highest total; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT order_number::text AS record, total FROM bus_purchase_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND total IS NOT NULL ORDER BY total DESC LIMIT 10
%%report purchase-order-line-quantity-per-month title: Average quantity per month entity: PurchaseOrderLine chart: line x: month y: average_quantity help: Itemized good or service ordered from a supplier. The average quantity of purchase order lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_quantity FROM bus_purchase_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report purchase-order-line-largest-by-quantity title: The ten largest purchase order lines by quantity entity: PurchaseOrderLine chart: bar x: record y: quantity help: Itemized good or service ordered from a supplier. The records with the highest quantity; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, quantity FROM bus_purchase_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND quantity IS NOT NULL ORDER BY quantity DESC LIMIT 10
%%report purchase-order-line-unit-price-per-month title: Average unit price per month entity: PurchaseOrderLine chart: line x: month y: average_unit_price help: Itemized good or service ordered from a supplier. The average unit price of purchase order lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(unit_price)::numeric, 2) AS average_unit_price FROM bus_purchase_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report purchase-order-line-largest-by-unit-price title: The ten largest purchase order lines by unit price entity: PurchaseOrderLine chart: bar x: record y: unit_price help: Itemized good or service ordered from a supplier. The records with the highest unit price; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, unit_price FROM bus_purchase_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND unit_price IS NOT NULL ORDER BY unit_price DESC LIMIT 10
