%%report approval-request-by-status title: Approval Requests by status entity: ApprovalRequest chart: pie x: status y: records help: Specific decision sought from a delegated authority, with rationale, decision and traceability to the business record. How approval requests divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_approval_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report approval-request-by-decision-type title: Approval Requests by decision type entity: ApprovalRequest chart: pie x: decision_type y: records help: Specific decision sought from a delegated authority, with rationale, decision and traceability to the business record. How approval requests divide across decision type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(decision_type::text, '(unset)') AS decision_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_approval_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report approval-request-lifecycle title: Approval Request lifecycle entity: ApprovalRequest chart: bar x: state y: records help: Specific decision sought from a delegated authority, with rationale, decision and traceability to the business record. Where approval requests sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'decision_pending' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'decision_under_review', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'decision_granted', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'decision_denied', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'decision_revision_required', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_approval_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report approval-request-created-per-month title: Approval Requests created per month entity: ApprovalRequest chart: line x: month y: records help: Specific decision sought from a delegated authority, with rationale, decision and traceability to the business record. New approval requests per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_approval_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
